This product includes code derived from Kev (https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev, Apache-2.0):
the input delimiters and escaping in sieve/encode.py and the confidence formulas in
sieve/api.py, with modifications. The model design follows Kev.

data/sieve-9b/ comes from Kev: decision_v7_train.jsonl is its decision-v7 training split
(Hugging Face dataset jaredpalmer/kev-suites, whose card states no licence), the two
date_policy files are from evals/night2/, and rule_structures.jsonl was generated with
Kev's rule generator (kev/composition.py).

decision_v7_train.jsonl contains text from ten public datasets, which keep the licences
stated on their Hugging Face cards; each record's _meta names its source, revision and row:
  cc-by-4.0      Banking77 (legacy-datasets/banking77)
  cc-by-sa-3.0   BoolQ (google/boolq), DBpedia-14 (fancyzhx/dbpedia_14)
  mixed          MultiNLI (nyu-mll/multi_nli: cc-by-3.0, cc-by-sa-3.0, mit, other)
  apache-2.0     Amazon Reviews en (SetFit/amazon_reviews_multi_en)
  other          IMDB (stanfordnlp/imdb), Yelp Review Full (Yelp/yelp_review_full)
  unknown        AG News (fancyzhx/ag_news), TREC (CogComp/trec)
  not stated     SST-5 (SetFit/sst5)
Check these licences before any commercial use of the data.
